cit ucid="JP-5254148-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5254148</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-58179655-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>58179655</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9085967-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9085967</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9290520-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9290520</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1103384A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>USUDA HIDENORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI, KOICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>USUDA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>USUDA HIDENORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>USUDA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>In an ink jet recording device (1), a fixed signal output section (461) sends to a head driving circuit (50) a signal, as a mode fixing signal (SP), indicating that ink droplets should not be discharged for nozzle openings (111) in a group not used for recording.  On the basis of the mode fixing signal (SP), the mode fixing circuit (18) of the head driving circuit (50) fixes the nozzle openings (111) in the corresponding group under the condition that they should not discharge ink droplets. Therefore, concerning the group that do not discharge ink droplets, there is no need to take the trouble to effect serial conversion and serial transfer of the data ("0" data) as recording data (S1), which data ("0") indicates that ink droplets should not be discharged, so that the wasteful processing time can be saved.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif d'enregistrement à jet d'encre (1) dans lequel une unité de sortie du signal fixe (461) envoie à un circuit de commande de la tête (50) un signal (en tant que signal de détermination des modes de déchargement (SP)) interdisant le déchargement des gouttelettes d'encre vers les ouvertures des buses (111) dans un groupe inactif pendant l'enregistrement. Sur la base du signal de détermination des modes de déchargement (SP), le circuit de détermination des modes de déchargement (18) du circuit de commande de la tête (50) prépare les ouvertures des buses (111) dans le groupe correspondant afin que celui-ci ne décharge pas des gouttelettes d'encre. Ainsi, pour ce qui concerne le groupe sensé être inactif, on peut s'épargner la peine d'effectuer une conversion sérielle et un transfert sériel des données (données "0") en tant que données d'enregistrement (S1), puisque ces données ("0") indiquent un état de non déchargement des gouttelettes d'encre qui peuvent faire économiser le temps de traitement excessif.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>